<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Royal Netherlands East Indies Army</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1830">1830</a>–<a href="/years/1950">1950</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as KNIL, Royal Netherlands Indies Army</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Royal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-indies">East Indies</a> Army (KNIL) was the colonial army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> East Indies, formed in 1830 and separate from the army of the Netherlands. Its soldiers were mainly Javanese, Ambonese and Manadonese under European officers, and it fought the Padri and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aceh">Aceh</a> wars that extended Dutch rule across the archipelago. Defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in 1942, it fought the Indonesian Republic after 1945 and was dissolved in 1950.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/royal-netherlands-east-indies-army.jpg" alt="Royal Netherlands East Indies Army" width="320" height="324" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Orange2000 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Royal_Netherlands_East_Indies_Army_Coat_of_Arms_Tentara_Kerajaan_Hindia_Belanda_Lambang_Koninklijk_Nederlandsch-Indisch_Leger_Wapenschil_Logo_KNIL.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
